{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>A cake as a terumah offering you shall lift up.</b> After the sin of the spies He required the hallah as well, so that they would be worthy that blessing rest upon their houses, as it says: וְרֵאשִׁית עֲרִיסוֹתֵיכֶם תִּתְּנוּ לַכֹּהֵן לְהָנִיחַ בְּרָכָה אֶל בֵּיתֶךָ (Ezekiel 44:30). And so Elijah: עֲשִׂי לִי מִשָּׁם עֻגָה קְטַנָּה בָרִאשׁוֹנָה וְהוֹצֵאת לִי, (וְלָךְ וְלִבְנֵךְ תַּעֲשִׂי בָאַחֲרוֹנָה,) כִּי כֹה אָמַר ה׳ כַּד הַקֶּמַח לֹא תִכְלָה (I Kings 17:13–14)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:57.750319604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}